1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Which evidence reaches the model?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,503
QueryTrace shows which source fragments can enter a model context — and why.

3
00:00:07,503 --> 00:00:12,445
Atlas Capital is a fictional workspace. Here, the guest is simulating an Analyst.

4
00:00:12,445 --> 00:00:17,458
Run returns 6 documents and 8 fragments. It retrieves context; it does not generate an
answer.

5
00:00:17,458 --> 00:00:22,512
2,013 estimated context tokens fit within the 2,048-token budget.

6
00:00:22,512 --> 00:00:31,078
Open the actual source. The fictional Form 10-K reports 34.2% ARR growth and 118% net
revenue retention.

7
00:00:31,078 --> 00:00:36,593
Decision Trace separates included, excluded and blocked fragments. A document can be
partially included.

8
00:00:36,593 --> 00:00:44,710
This fragment requires VP access. The simulated Analyst cannot include it under Full
Policy.

9
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:51,212
Same question, same role: the unfiltered Top-k baseline includes 2 documents that Full
Policy blocks.

10
00:00:51,212 --> 00:00:56,809
Top-k uses 2,390 estimated tokens; Full Policy uses 2,013. Their selection limits
differ.

11
00:00:56,809 --> 00:01:00,876
Export JSON preserves the executed query, role, metrics and decisions for inspection
outside the interface.

12
00:01:00,876 --> 00:01:09,443
All 12 configured PE queries completed. This benchmark reports no unauthorized
returns; it is not a production guarantee.

13
00:01:09,443 --> 00:01:17,005
Audit records the workspace, identity, effective role and policy. These local records
reset when the server restarts.

14
00:01:17,005 --> 00:01:21,690
The demo accounts have different access. Sign in as Julia to use an authenticated
Analyst role.

15
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:28,256
Julia’s document role is enforced by the server. It is no longer a guest simulation.

16
00:01:28,256 --> 00:01:35,458
Documents exposes the six sources Julia may read. The other ten documents are withheld
from this account.

17
00:01:35,458 --> 00:01:42,983
Nimbus has its own corpus, roles and scenarios. Switching workspaces clears the
previous result.

18
00:01:42,983 --> 00:01:49,485
Guide walks through the same real workflow. Optional Ask can generate an answer when a
provider is configured.

19
00:01:49,485 --> 00:01:53,485
An auditable context gateway · Fictional demo data
